  "text": "<p>Every question generates a new random variant each time you ask for one. A question is worth 6 points: 2 for the first correct variant, and more for consecutive correct variants. You get 3 tries per variant; after a submission a second hint unlocks and the full worked solution is shown once you have used your tries or answered correctly.</p><p>Lectures 18–21: ideal D/A reconstruction, digital filtering of analog signals (A/D → H<sub>d</sub> → D/A), aliasing, the DFT, zero padding, modulo indexing, DFT properties and circular convolution. DFT spectral analysis is still ahead of the lectures; it follows the recent Midterm 2 keys.</p>",
